 CBProbe args;want;got;bad;i;n
⍝ Hammer the synchronous WG round-trip and report whether every reply came
⍝ back to the session that asked for it.
⍝
⍝ Mechanism under test: eWG blocks the session thread in
⍝ `WG_TIMEOUT ⎕TGET token` (WaitForWG.aplf:7) while EWC's Listen thread
⍝ deposits the browser's reply with `⎕TPUT token` (Handler.aplf:75). Both
⍝ sides compute token←WG_TOKENBASE+TOKENSTEP×1⌈ID×MODE=2 — per-session
⍝ under Multi. If that routing is wrong, a reply lands in the wrong
⍝ session's ⎕TGET and this reads back another clone's name.
⍝
⍝ F1.TOKEN is an Edit because only dynamic properties actually go to the
⍝ browser; a Label's Caption would be answered locally and prove nothing.

 n←8
 want←⍕⎕THIS
 bad←''

 :Trap 0
     :For i :In ⍳n
         got←∊'F1.TOKEN'eWG'Text'
         :If got≢want
             bad,←' ',got
         :EndIf
         ⍝ Form Size is dynamic too — extra traffic to widen the window in
         ⍝ which a concurrent session's reply could be mis-delivered.
         {}'F1'eWG'Size'
     :EndFor

     :If 0=≢bad
         'F1.PROBE'eWS'Caption'('OK ',want,' x',⍕n)
     :Else
         'F1.PROBE'eWS'Caption'('CROSSED ',want,' got:',bad)
     :EndIf
 :Else
     ⍝ A WG timeout signals 6 from WaitForWG.aplf:11. Surface it as text so
     ⍝ the test fails with a diagnosis instead of hanging.
     'F1.PROBE'eWS'Caption'('ERROR ',∊⊃⎕DMX.DM)
 :EndTrap
